    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1198">

                <pb facs="0983" n="973" xml:id="pg973"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.633/8–1349: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jones</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-08-13">August 13,
                        1949</date>.<lb/>[Received August 13—3:48 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1780. Reference Embtel 1223 [<hi rendition="#italic">1723</hi>], August 6.
                    Following is Mukden telegram 29, August 9 to Embassy: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Exit permits requested for 10 American staff members, 5 American and 2
                            alien dependents Mukden–Shanghai. Travel permits requested for 3 FSA
                            employees; no date departure Mukden specified, but shall set date
                            soonest possible.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Sent Department 1780; repeated Shanghai 985, OffEmb Canton 746.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jones</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
